    details: `Day 01: ARRIVE CHENNAI

Arrive in Chennai late evening and meet our representative at airport, who will transfer you to your hotel. Capital of the southeastern state of Tamil Nadu, Chennai is one of the four major metropolitan cities in India.

Day 02: TO KANCHEEPURAM & MAHABALIPURAM (140 KMS)

After relaxing in the morning and overcoming the jetlag, enjoy a late morning tour of Chennai city. Visit MARINA BEACH, ST. GEORGE FORT, SAN THOME Cathedral, and KAPALESHWAR TEMPLE. Then drive to KANCHIPURAM, the fabled city of a thousand temples. Continue to Mahabalipuram for overnight at your beach resort.

Day 03: IN MAHABALIPURAM

Mahabalipuram with its picturesque location is renowned for its series of charming RATHAS and the spectacular carved relief depicting ARJUNA'S PENANCE. The magnificent SHORE TEMPLE built by king Rajasimha in the seventh century houses the shrines of both Shiva and Vishnu. Visit the Varaha Cave and KRISHNA MANDAPAM. Return to your hotel late in the afternoon for overnight stay.

Day 04: TO PONDICHERRY (140 KMS)

After breakfast drive to Pondicherry (or Puducheri) meaning 'the new settlement'. It was a French settlement. On arrival check in at your city hotel. During your afternoon tour visit SRI AUROBINDO ASHRAM, the PONDICHERRY MUSEUM, and the pleasant beach alongside promenade.

Day 05: TO TANJORE VIA CHIDAMBARAM

We drive to Tanjore. En route visit CHIDAMBRAM, famous for its NATARAJA TEMPLE. Arrive Tanjore in the afternoon to check in at your hotel. Visit the BRIHADEESWARA TEMPLE, the wonderful PALACE, ART GALLERY and the SARASWATI MAHAL LIBRARY.

Day 06: TO TRICHY (55 kms)

Visit Trichy in the morning. In Trichy visit ROCK FORT, VINAYAKA TEMPLE, SRI THAYUMANASWAMY TEMPLE, TIRUVANAIKKAVAL or JAMBUKESWARA TEMPLE, and SRIRANGAM - the most important pilgrim center on an island, home to the gigantic SRI RANGANATHA TEMPLE with 22 gopurams.

Day 07: TO MADURAI

Drive 4 hours today to Madurai in Tamil Nadu. One of the oldest cities in South India, Madurai has been the centre of learning and pilgrimage for centuries. In the afternoon visit the city. The Meenakshi-Sundareswarar temple is located at the heart of the city - an outstanding example of Vijayanagar temple architecture with four entrances and spectacular gopurams covered in multi-coloured images.

Day 08: TO MUNNAR

Breakfast is followed by drive to MUNNAR. Surrounded by lush green tea and coffee plantations, Munnar is a picturesque hill station situated in the eastern part of Kerala. The town is located at the confluence of three mountain streams and is known for its clean, neat ambience. The beautiful landscapes and cosy weather make Munnar one of the most sought-after destinations in South India.

Day 09: IN MUNNAR

Visit important sites including Pothamedu, Devikulam, Pallivasal, Attukal, Nyayamakad, Mettupetty, Rajamala (natural habitat of endangered Nilgiri Tahr), Chitthirapuram, and Echo Point.

Day 10: TO PERIYAR

This morning travel approximately 4 hours to Thekkady, the main entrance to Periyar Wildlife Sanctuary. Upon arrival check-into your cottage. The wildlife sanctuary is the natural habitat of a wide variety of animal species. The Periyar Lake is a paradise for nature lovers and a birdwatcher's delight. The greatest attraction is the herds of wild elephants that come down to play in the lake.

Day 11: TO KUMARAKOM

Enjoy an early morning boat ride on Lake Periyar! Periyar is one of the largest and most frequently visited wildlife reserves in India. Return for breakfast then visit spice plantations. Later drive approximately 3 hours to Kumarakom. An old rubber plantation set around the Vembanad Lake has been developed into a bird sanctuary. Your overnight stay is at Kumarakom Lake Resort, a heritage resort on the banks of Vembanad Lake.

Day 12: TO ALLEPPEY and TO COCHIN

After breakfast make a short trip to the ferry point where you board your houseboat. Reserved is a private, one room houseboat that travels until sunset when it anchors for the night at Alleppey. The houseboat has a private balcony, fully furnished rooms with attached bathrooms, and an experienced cook for authentic Kerala cuisine. Later switch over to your car in Alleppey and drive to your hotel in Cochin.

Day 13: IN COCHIN

Enjoy a guided tour in the first half of the day. The city has three distinctive regions – Ernakulam, Mattancherry and Fort Cochin. Our walking tour will take us to Jew Town including the Pardesi Synagogue; the Mattancherry Palace (Dutch Palace); Fort Cochin; the Chinese Fishing Nets on the northern shore; and St Francis Church. A highlight is watching the fishermen working the nets as the sun is setting.

Day 14: COCHIN / DEPARTURE

Transfer to airport to connect your onward flight to Mumbai or to any other destination.`,
