    details: `Day 01: ARRIVE DELHI

On arrival at Delhi's international airport, we will be met by our representative and taken to your hotel for overnight stay. Living testament to the glory of the Mughal days, patron of palaces and tombs and the capital of India, New Delhi is all of this and more. Delhi is as modern or ancient as you want it to be.

Day 02: IN DELHI

Full day guided city tour of New Delhi and Old Delhi. In New Delhi visit the Qutab Minar, Humayun's Tomb, India Gate, President House, Parliament and Government Secretariat buildings. In Old Delhi visit the historic Red Fort - Shah Jehan's elegant citadel in red sandstone. Very near the Fort is the Jama Masjid (Friday Mosque), India's largest mosque. Take an interesting rickshaw ride through the famous bazaars of Chandni Chowk. Also visit Raj Ghat - the memorial to Mahatma Gandhi.

Day 03: DELHI / AGRA

Drive to Agra (204 km/ 3.5 hrs) late in the morning. Stop at SIKANDRA, Akbar's memorial at the entrance of the city. The monument built of red sandstone is quite a sight to behold. The tomb is a combination of Muslim and Hindu architectural styles. The building of red sandstone is four-storeys tall, approximately 31 metres in height.

Day 04: IN AGRA

Today visit the Taj Mahal - the inimitable poem in white marble. Built over a period of 22 years, by the Mughal Emperor Shah Jahan in 1630, for his Queen Mumtaz Mahal to enshrine her mortal remains, it is one of the seven modern wonders of the World. Also visit the Agra Fort, built by three Mughal Emperors starting from Akbar the Great in 1565 AD, which is a masterpiece of design and construction. Within the fort are a number of exquisite buildings including the Moti Masjid, Jahangir's Palace, Khaas Mahal and the Sheesh Mahal, Diwane-i-Am, Diwane-i-Khas and Musamman Burj.

Day 05: AGRA / SIKRI / BHARATPUR BIRD SANCTUARY / JAIPUR

After early breakfast, drive 38kms to the deserted city of Fatehpur Sikri. This exquisite city built by Akbar the Great in 1569, in red sandstone; with its forts, palaces and mosques was abandoned 14 years after its creation. The Diwan-i-am, Diwan-i-khas, Pachisi court, Jodha Bhai's Palace, Mariam's Palace, Birbal's Palace, Hawa Mahal and Panch Mahal are some of the important buildings. The Friday Mosque and the exquisite tomb of Sheik Salim Chisti are in the religious grounds.

Drive another 18kms to Bharatpur - one of Asia's finest Bird sanctuaries, the Keoladeo Ghana National Park. The sanctuary is a haven and home to over 400 kinds of birds. Travel by bicycle or cycle-rickshaw with a local guide. Continue your drive to JAIPUR and arrive the capital of Rajasthan by late afternoon. Rest of the day is free to relax.

Day 06: IN JAIPUR

This morning drive 11kms to visit AMBER FORT, the ancient capital of the State until 1728. Visit the Temple of Kali, the Hall of Victory or Jai Mahal and Jagmandir. You can have the unique experience of traveling on elephant back to and from the top of the hill. During your tour of the pink city, visit the CITY PALACE - the former royal residence with a superb collection of Rajasthani costumes and armoury. Also visit the JANTAR MANTAR - an astrological and astronomical Observatory built by Maharaja Jai Singh. Lastly stop at PALACE-OF-WINDS and spend time in crowded lanes of pink city. Return to your hotel for overnight stay.

Day 07: TO JODHPUR

Today fly to Jodhpur. Situated at an altitude of about 125 metres, THE MEHRANGARH FORT is spread over an area of 5 sq. km in the heart of the city. The fort has seven gates - Jayapol, Fatehpol and Lohapol. Inside the fort, a series of courtyards and palaces greet the visitor. Visit JASWANT THADA: a white marble memorial built in memory of Maharaja Jaswant II in 1899. UMAID BHAWAN PALACE: Made of marble and pink sandstone, the construction started in 1929 and it took 16 years to complete. This majestic building is presently the residence of the former rulers with a part of it running as hotel and remaining part as a museum. Overnight is at the hotel.

Day 08: TO UDAIPUR and to DELWARA

Fly this morning to UDAIPUR - the city of lakes, also known as "the Venice of the East". Founded by Maharana Udai Singh in 1568, and considered the jewel of Mewar, Udaipur's air is filled with a strong sense of romance and the best of Rajputana. On arrival you will be transferred to DEVIGARH PALACE in DELWARA for a 4-night stay.

Day 09: IN DELWARA

Full day is at leisure to relax by the poolside or to enjoy the spa in the resort.

Day 10: IN DELWARA

After breakfast visit the famous temples of EKLINGJI & NAGDA on the way to Udaipur city. Eklingji Temple is dedicated to Shiva, regarded as the guardian deity of the Mewar. Nagda has three ruined Jain temples—Adbhutji Temple and the Vaishnavite Sas-Bahu Temples—all dating back to the 11th century. Continue your drive to Udaipur. During a guided tour visit the CITY PALACE built in 1725, JAGDISH TEMPLE built in 1651, FATEH SAGAR and SAHELIYON KI BARI. In the evening enjoy a leisurely boat ride on LAKE PICHOLA.

Day 11: TO UDAIPUR

This morning drive through valleys in the remote Aravalli Range to RANAKPUR to visit one of the most important Jain temples in India. This marble complex has 29 halls supported by 1,444 pillars, each adorned with hundreds of carved figures, no two alike. Visit KUMBHALGARH - one of the finest examples of defensive fortifications in Rajasthan. The Kumbhalgarh Wildlife Sanctuary is situated to the west of the fort. Finish the day in Udaipur and stay there for overnight in one of the palace hotels.

Day 12: TO MUMBAI

Drive 22 kms to Udaipur airport today to take a short flight to Mumbai. Mumbai is the fast paced commercial, financial, industrial and celluloid capital of India. Visit the Gateway of India, Mani Bhawan or the Gandhi memorial, Prince of Wales Museum, Marine Drive and Juhu. The Hanging Garden and the Kamla Nehru Garden will provide rest between your sightseeing trips and Chowpatty gives you the view of one of the most happening beaches of Mumbai.

Day 13: DEPARTURE

You will be transferred today to the International airport for your onward flight. End of our services.`,
